traneous changes were made.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with status field, atomically cancelling order and its CREATED shipments while preventing cancellation if any shipment is CONFIRMED, rejecting future shipment creation for cancelled orders, and making repeated cancel idempotent.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum and status field\n              OrderController.kt — Added cancel() endpoint and ShipmentRepository injection\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId() method\n              ShipmentController.kt — Added order status check when creating shipment and OrderRepository injection\n              ApiError.kt — Added ORDER_CONFLICT error code\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — Added tests for cancel endpoint, status field, and atomic shipment cancellation\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Updated existing tests to create orders and added tests for order status validation\n\nTests         `creates an order with ACTIVE status` — verifies orders start in ACTIVE state\n              `cancels an ACTIVE order and transitions to CANCELLED` — verifies cancel endpoint returns updated order\n              `cancels all CREATED shipments when cancelling order` — verifies shipments are atomically cancelled with order\n              `cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds and changes nothing` — verifies idempotent cancel\n              `cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing` — verifies all-or-nothing constraint\n              `cancelling a non-existent order returns 404` — verifies error handling\n              `creates a shipment for a non-existent order with existing behaviour` — verifies no regression for missing orders\n              `rejects creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order with 409` — verifies shipment creation prevention\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS — Tests